  "performance_interpretation": [
    "Fewer draw submissions do not prove improved FPS. The controlled furnished hall reduced315 to205 calls; the unchanged native household peak reduced281 to185. Native full lifecycle completed178.219s versus189.89s before, but loading/cache noise and vsync prevent treating that as a guaranteed speedup.",
    "The matched short software-renderer baseline sample was408.053ms before and431.371ms after, despite237 to157 calls. The additional warm bounce and different runner conditions require further isolation. Continuous software rendering still fails240s; do not report the total CI run as green.",
    "The final ordinary world120-frame medium sample is42.586ms (about23.5fps), compared with the earlier roughly19fps sample. Short windows and background/cache variation do not establish a lighting-caused speedup or stable30fps game."
  ],
  "failures_and_retries": [
    "The first independent sole observer reconnected the same modifier callback when the loaded world reentered the tree. Game actions reached their success marker, but the diagnostic emitted an ERROR and is not treated as a clean pass. Added an idempotent connection guard and repeated the whole ordinary-input scenario.",
    "First profiling helper attempted an ArrayMesh-only method on BoxMesh; own failed process was stopped, the diagnostic switched to general surface arrays and was rerun.",
    "The first new room fixture had GDScript inference errors, then placed the player before Player._ready restored its saved starting position. Fixed fixture setup order; only initial fixture placement is used afterward.",
    "An invented75s local wrapper deadline stopped furniture validation near its final stage. The original repository gate is180s with a130s simulation watchdog; rerun with those unchanged project limits passed100.656s. The75s result remains recorded under build.",
    "First working-root room review completed its assertions but exited3221225477. A matching Windows Application event at2026-10-25 12:52:19 named Intel ig9icd64.dll31.0.101.2140, exception0xc0000005. It is a failed run. After actual per-preset frames and deferred destruction/readback, two working-root repeats exited0; this does not prove all Intel driver crashes fixed.",
    "The source-only diagnostic workflow needed a branch push trigger because GitHub had not registered workflow_dispatch for the new off-default workflow. No mandatory gate was skipped."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Human models, garment seams, hair, arm/leg naturalness and full concept art acceptance remain open; this package changes no human geometry.",
    "Rooms still require richer architectural/furniture/art work; the existing atlas fabric response is subtle, not a new photorealistic textile set.",
    "The local household doorway fixture uses the production square/home/people and real physics/save state, but its isolated background and dressing coverage are not the full city. The separate room review includes the production decorator and a grounded player.",
    "Native own profiles preserve user settings/saves; this is automated testing, not manual play or a new complete world traversal.",
    "The earlier ordinary-world run still printed89 ObjectDB leaks at exit. No global shutdown or leak fix is claimed.",
    "Main remains unchanged; no stable installer publication, force push or shared-index reset. Shared checkout remains dirty because unrelated work is preserved."
  ],
  "references": [
    {
      "source": "User-supplied house/world concept boards",
      "decision": "Keep warm fixture-local light, physically separated rooms, furniture and supported human scale; no change of visual direction."
